----- SOURCE CODE
-- one.i
fn two() { 2 }

-- main.i
import one.{two}

pub fn main() {
  two
}

----- ERROR
error: Use of private value
  ┌─ /src/one/two.i:1:13
  │
1 │ import one.{two}
  │             ^^^

`one` does define `two`, but it is private and cannot be accessed by other
modules.

error: Unknown variable
  ┌─ /src/one/two.i:4:3
  │
4 │   two
  │   ^^^

The name `two` is not in scope here.
